.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL-PRIME 1ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openssl-prime
.Nd compute prime numbers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm openssl prime
.Oo
.Fl help ]
.Oo
.Fl hex ]
.Oo
.Fl generate ]
.Oo
.Fl bits
.Em num ]
.Oo
.Fl safe ]
.Oo
.Fl provider
.Em name ]
.Oo
.Fl provider-path
.Em path ]
.Oo
.Fl provparam
.Em [name:]key=value ]
.Oo
.Fl propquery
.Em propq ]
.Oo
.Fl checks
.Em num ]
.Oo
.Em number
.Oc
\&...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command checks if the specified numbers are prime.
.Pp
If no numbers are given on the command line, the
.Sy -generate
flag should be used to generate primes according to the requirements
specified by the rest of the flags.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Display an option summary.
.It Sy -hex
Generate hex output.
.It Sy -generate
Generate a prime number.
.It Sy -bits Em num
Generate a prime with
.Em num
bits.
.It Sy -safe
When used with
.Sy -generate ,
generates a "safe" prime.
If the number generated is
.Em n ,
then check that
.Qo Li ( Ns Em n Ns -1)/2 Qc
is also prime.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.It Sy -checks Em num
This parameter is ignored.
.El
